  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Satay chicken serves 4 and takes about 35 minutes plus at least 1 hour marinating. The chicken marinates in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "lemongrass",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "lemongrass"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "coconut milk",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "coconut-milk"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " before grilling. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "peanut",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "peanuts-roasted"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " dipping sauce comes together in 5 minutes. Turmeric in the marinade (no slug, described below) gives the skewers their golden colour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "If using wooden skewers, soak them in cold water for at least 30 minutes before threading so they do not burn under the grill."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
